WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.310
- Welcome to the Huberman Lab Podcast,

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.920
where we discuss science
and science-based tools

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.138
for everyday life.

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:09.390
[upbeat music]

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.410
I'm Andrew Huberman,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.410
and I'm a professor of
neurobiology and ophthalmology

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.330
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.970
Today, we are going to
discuss your brain chemistry

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.850
and how to control and
optimize your brain chemistry

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.860
for all aspects of mental health,

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.140
physical health, and performance.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.570
Many times before on the
Huberman Lab Podcast,

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.840
and frankly, every time I'm
a guest on another podcast,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.720
I get questions about science
and science-based tools

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.580
for things like enhancing sleep,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.780
enhancing focus,

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.950
enhancing creativity,

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.090
improving relationships,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.520
getting over grief and on and on,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.260
all of which are valid questions

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.020
and for which there are protocols
that are based in science

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.350
and that work the first
time and every time.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.350
However far more important
than knowing a protocol

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.050
is understanding why a
given protocol works.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.000
That's why I'm always
hammering on mechanism

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.520
and explaining the cells
and circuits and chemicals,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.110
at least to some detail,

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.110
so that people can understand
not just what to do,

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.970
but why it works and therefore,

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.740
how to change a protocol

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.570
as their life circumstances change,

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.310
or as goals change.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.190
Now today we are going to
go even a layer deeper.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.200
We're going to explore the foundations

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.200
of your biology in your brain and body

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.390
that allow any protocol to work

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.040
because as it turns out,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.480
all of the protocols out there,

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.100
whether or not it's a breathing protocol

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.800
or a supplement or a prescription drug

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.630
or an exercise routine,

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.570
they all tap into and leverage

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:37.350
a core set of just a few
biological mechanisms.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.183
That's right,

00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:41.460
beneath everything you
are able to do and feel

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.220
and indeed beneath every
protocol that allows you

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.690
to change for the better

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.160
and optimize your mental health,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.900
physical health, and performance,

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.910
there's just a small subset of chemicals

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.670
that you're leveraging toward that change.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.900
So today we are going to talk

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.750
about the four major
pillars of neurochemistry

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.790
that allow you to, for instance,

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.710
be focused when you want to focus,

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.910
that allow you to relax

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.800
when you need to relax and de-stress,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.960
that allow you to optimize your sleep,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.020
that allow you to optimize
your exercise routine

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.750
or to work through a pain
point in relationship

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.930
or in career or in your
relationship to yourself.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.100
So what I can say for sure

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.380
is that by the end of this episode,

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.870
you will have a much richer understanding

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.180
about how your brain and nervous system

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.250
and indeed your entire body work.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.680
And you'll have a much
firmer understanding

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.770
as to which protocols
and tools to reach for

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.740
given your particular goals in the moment,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.740
in the day, across the
week, across the month,

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.770
across the year, and indeed
across your entire lifespan.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.440
So what we're really going
for today are principles,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.340
deeper understanding of why
any given protocol works

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.520
and we are also going to
discuss specific protocols.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.380
Some of those protocols I've discussed

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.110
on previous episodes of
the Huberman Lab Podcast,

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.340
but I must say,

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.500
many of the protocols and
tools that I will discuss

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.510
are brand new and based on research

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.160
that I have not discussed at all,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.520
simply because the research
papers came out only recently,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.820
or these are papers that
I only recently unearthed.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.340
In fact, I'm going to share
with you two recent studies

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.160
in a moment that are exceedingly important

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.660
for optimizing your sleep

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.370
and these are studies that, again,

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.520
I've never discussed
in any episode on sleep

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.870
or on any other podcast.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.310
So by the end of today's episode,

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.660
you're going to have far more knowledge

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.420
about your biology and psychology
than you did at the start

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.460
and you'll be armed with many more tools

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.690
and most importantly,

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.730
principles so that you can navigate

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.160
not just the tools
presented on this podcast,

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.800
but in the vast landscape
of tools that are out there

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.470
for mental health, physical
health and performance.

